ern "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "coming from Europe and North America"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You can have a Western breakfast."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le16ob03aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "Chinese"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "relating to China"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You could have a Chinese breakfast as well."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le16ob03aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "combination "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "two or more different things that can be put together"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We also offer a combination breakfast."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le16ob03aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to depart"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to leave"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  The bus departs from the hotel at 9 a.m."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le16ob03aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to cover"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to include"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  The tour covers The Great Wall of China and the Forbidden City. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le16ob03aud04"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn4le16ob03re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Talking About Intentions and Plans"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Continuous</span> and <span class=\"strong\">be going to</span> to talk about future actions and events. <br/><br/>    You use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Continuous</span> to talk about arrangements and plans. <span class=\"strong\">Be going to</span> puts an emphasis on the idea of intention (decide to do something). <br/>    Examples: <br><span class=\"italic\"> <ul><li>We are departing from the hotel at 9 a.m.</span></li><li><span class=\"italic\">We are going to return around 5 p.m.</span></li> <li>The bus is leaving in 10 minutes. </li>    <li> We're traveling to Beijing next week. These are the tickets. </li>     <li>I'm going to visit Paris next year.</li>      <li>He's going to visit all the museums and monuments.</li></ul><br/></span>   You can use <span class=\"strong\">intend to</span> in place of <span class=\"strong\">be going to</span>. <br/>   Example: <span class=\"italic\">I intend to arrive early.</span><br><br>Remember that you need to conjugate the auxiliary verb TO BE for both the Present Continuous and be going to."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Go on the internet."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Research a tour you can take in Beijing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make sure you research the tour in English."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Answer these questions: <ul><li>How many days is it?</li> <li> What places do you go to?</li> <li>What things do you do?</li> <li>What transportation do you use?</li></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": " Share your answers with your class."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I research about an overseas tour."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I locate specific information to answer questions."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I communicate my information to a group."}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"id": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn4le16ob03re2aud01", "cover